{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA (complete; investigation only)\n\nOBSERVATION\nThe ticket reports that `attach_commits` successfully recorded merged SHA `ea394c34...` on `goldfilled-portly-dungbeetle`, but the close precheck still failed with “no commit references it.” Code inspection matches: attached commits are read by `_attached_commit_shas`, but not considered by the presence check that decides whether work “landed.”\n\nHYPOTHESIS\n`src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:_check_work_landed` computes `referencing = _referencing_commits(...)` and raises when `own_impact and not referencing`. The function calls `_check_file_impact_vs_diff(...)` only after that raise point. The attached-commit source is unioned later inside `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:_check_file_impact_vs_diff`, so attachments can validate diff impact but cannot satisfy the earlier “at least one landed commit exists” predicate.\n\nCONFIRMATION\nConfirmed with a deterministic monkeypatch experiment: `_union_file_impact` and `field_reads.file_impact` returned `['src/a.py']`, `_referencing_commits` returned `[]`, `_attached_commit_shas` returned `['attached-sha']`, and `_check_file_impact_vs_diff` was instrumented. `_check_work_landed(...)` raised the existing “no commit references it” error and the diff checker was never called (`DIFF_CALLS 0`). This would have been disproven if the attached SHA had been unioned into the presence decision or if the diff checker had run.\n\nSUGGESTED FIX DIRECTION\nMake `_check_work_landed` decide presence over the union of trailer-discovered commits and valid attached commits, while keeping the existing asymmetric unreadable-SHA policy and the later file-impact validation over both sources."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788737387721494001,"uuid":"03e61734-94c5-4c36-ac31-f781ad8231c1"}